{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018ATuw59FhBG1oCSNQRRwfS","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"hash":"6e4cdcd9db634a947b317df793d5b8170a9768e9","date":"2026-09-17T20:43:12+05:30","message":"(feat) Add date range filter to bills table (#831)","refs":"","body":"* (feat) Add date range filter to bills table\n\n* (feat) Guard inverted date range and show Clear dates only when a date is set\n\nSkip the bill fetch when the end date is before the start date and show\nthe picker's invalid text instead, since the backend rejects that range\nwith a 400. Render the Clear dates button only when a date is set. Raise\nthe billing backend floor to 2.5.0-0, which is the version that adds the\nstartDate and endDate search parameters.\n\n* (fix) Skip the bills request for an inverted date range and let the date controls wrap","authorName":"Nethmi Rodrigo","authorEmail":"nethmi@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"e8126b39dc10bcdc719250b004afe86f7782f36a","date":"2026-06-04T14:23:05+05:30","message":"(feat) O3-5413: Add bill refunds (#738)","refs":"","body":"* feat(refunds): add bill refunds feature\n\n- Cashiers can request refunds on PAID/PARTIALLY_REFUNDED bills; admins approve or reject; cashiers then process approved refunds to COMPLETED\n- Supports bill-level and line-item-scoped refunds with cumulative cap enforcement; at most one active refund per scope at a time\n- Adds admin Refund Requests page, cashier Request Refund modal, and admin Review Bill Refunds modal with receipt rail showing approved and completed refund totals\n- Fixes: REJECTED refunds were incorrectly reducing remainingRefundable; COMPLETED refunds were not deducted from line-item remaining (double-refund risk); bill.refunds?.filter().reduce() crashed when refunds was undefined\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(refunds): add pending refunds filter to bills table\n\nAdds REFUND_REQUESTED to BillStatus and a 'Pending refunds' filter option in the bills table to surface bills awaiting refund processing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(refunds): address SonarCloud issues in refunds feature\n\n- Extract deeply nested onRefundRequest/onClick callbacks into named functions\n- Replace chained ternaries with if/else block before JSX return\n- Add null guard in handleRequestRefund to remove non-null assertions\n- Use flatMap for type-safe lineItemUuid set construction\n- Remove unnecessary `as RefundStatus` cast (type already narrows correctly)\n- Replace role=\"progressbar\" on div with aria-busy=\"true\"\n- Mark component props interfaces as readonly\n- Replace window with globalThis in test files\n- Remove unused showSnackbar and useOpenmrsFetchAll imports\n- Replace parseFloat with Number.parseFloat\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(refunds): remove unnecessary non-null assertion in handleLineItemRefundRequest\n\nAdd early return guard for item.uuid so TypeScript narrows the type,\nmaking the ! assertion redundant and satisfying SonarCloud S4325.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(refunds): keep review modal open on action and fix multi-line refund eligibility\n\n- Review modal now refreshes bill data in place instead of closing after approve/reject\n- Bills in REFUND_REQUESTED status can now accept refund requests on unaffected line items\n- Add unit tests covering all refund eligibility scenarios (bill-level and line-level blocking)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(refunds): mock billing.resource in review-bill-refunds modal test\n\nuseBill was added to the modal but the test's esm-framework mock did not\nexpose openmrsFetch, causing the test suite to fail on push.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(refunds): resolve duplicate translation key and add voided discount test\n\n- Align refundAmount translation value to 'Refund amount' across all usages\n- Add test asserting voided discounts are not rendered in DiscountsTable\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(refunds): add void action to refund review card\n\nAdmins can now void any refund regardless of status. Follows the same\ninline-confirm pattern as the discount card's delete action.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(refunds): improve refund review modal and validation\n\n- Rename `busy` → `processingRefundId`/`disabled` in RefundCard and RefundReviewStack for clearer semantics\n- Add per-line-item refund cap validation before approving\n- Fix over-approval guard to exclude the refund being approved from committed total\n- Show progress bar alongside content instead of replacing it during loading\n- Add inline error state when bill data fails to load\n- Guard against null netAmount in invoice refund handler\n- Switch requestRefundModal and reviewBillRefundsModal to async lifecycle\n- Make MappedBill.netAmount non-optional\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(refunds): reconcile summary card figures when discount and prior refunds exist\n\nShow amountAfterDiscount as the bill-level scope total in the summary card, and\nadd an 'Already refunded' row (hidden when zero) so all three figures always\nadd up visually regardless of discounts or prior refunds on the same bill.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Cleanup props\n\n* feat(refunds): show tooltip on disabled Request refund button\n\nWraps the button in a Carbon Tooltip (only when disabled) to explain\nthat a line-item refund is already in progress, and adds unit tests\ncovering the disabled state and tooltip label.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(refunds): surface void as delete in UI and add coverage for line-item and void flows\n\nReplaces all user-facing \"void\" language with \"delete\" to match the\nconvention used for discounts, line items, and bills. Adds tests for\nline-item-scoped refund approval (including the exceeds-line-total\nguard) and the full delete confirmation flow.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(refunds): show already-refunded row for line items with prior completed refunds\n\nComputes alreadyRefunded symmetrically for line-item refunds using\nscopeTotal - remainingRefundable, matching the bill-level calculation.\nThe summary card now shows the \"Already refunded\" row whenever a line\nitem has prior completed refunds, making the figures add up correctly.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(refunds): close concurrent-action races and i18n gaps\n\n- Disable Approve/Confirm reject/Confirm delete across all cards while\n  any request is in flight (was only guarding the active card's UUID)\n- Add tests covering cross-card Approve and Confirm-reject lock-out\n- Remove dead useBillRefunds export and its test block\n- Add extraction hint block + en.json keys for all BillStatus values\n  so the receipt-rail status tag never falls back to raw enum strings\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(refunds): remove redundant non-null assertions flagged by SonarCloud\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(refunds): suppress false invalid state on empty NumberInput on open\n\nAdd allowEmpty to the NumberInput in the refund and discount modals so\nCarbon's internal emptiness check does not trigger the red invalid state\nbefore the user has typed anything. Submit gating is unaffected.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(refunds): keep confirmation footer contained at narrow modal widths\n\nSplit confirmation copy from its button group into a wrapping flex row so\nthe text and controls stack vertically rather than overflow at narrow widths.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","authorName":"Nethmi Rodrigo","authorEmail":"nethmi@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"276998ab31efde52652f58a4a22e099970ca615f","date":"2026-05-06T03:05:16+05:30","message":"(feat) Default bills table filter to \"Pending confirmation\" (#727)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Nethmi Rodrigo","authorEmail":"nethmi@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"6e3d447cbfade14f3ec4b73d1697daf8f203bf79","date":"2026-02-13T16:17:05+05:30","message":"(fix) Delete line items from a bill (#617)","refs":"","body":"The billing tables had several inconsistencies: the \"Visit time\" column\nwas misleadingly named (it's actually `dateCreated`), there was no\nreceipt/invoice number column for navigating to invoices, the patient\nname was a link to the invoice page (unintuitive), and the billed items\ndisplay had a trailing \"&\" when a line item lacked a name.\n\n- Rename \"Visit time\" to \"Bill date\" across all billing tables\n- Add \"Invoice number\" column linking to the invoice page in the bill\n  list, bill history, and patient bills tables\n- Remove clickable link from patient name in the bill list table\n- Rename \"Bill code\" to \"Invoice number\" in the invoice line items table\n- Fix trailing \"&\" in billed items by replacing reduce with\n  map/filter/join\n- Update unit tests and e2e tests to reflect the new column structure\n","authorName":"Nethmi Rodrigo","authorEmail":"nethmi@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"e734a4221aead9c6787cec024a58782c84452cb7","date":"2026-02-07T01:56:14+03:00","message":"(fix) Add invoice number column and fix billed items display","refs":"","body":"The billing tables had several inconsistencies: the \"Visit time\" column\nwas misleadingly named (it's actually `dateCreated`), there was no\nreceipt/invoice number column for navigating to invoices, the patient\nname was a link to the invoice page (unintuitive), and the billed items\ndisplay had a trailing \"&\" when a line item lacked a name.\n\n- Rename \"Visit time\" to \"Bill date\" across all billing tables\n- Add \"Invoice number\" column linking to the invoice page in the bill\n  list, bill history, and patient bills tables\n- Remove clickable link from patient name in the bill list table\n- Rename \"Bill code\" to \"Invoice number\" in the invoice line items table\n- Fix trailing \"&\" in billed items by replacing reduce with\n  map/filter/join\n- Update unit tests and e2e tests to reflect the new column structure\n","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"a71eed142190dcdab9199d02e27bc1ef49d71933","date":"2025-11-24T18:15:29+05:30","message":"(fix) Use server-side pagination when fetching bills (#504)","refs":"","body":"* (fix): Use pagination when fetching bills\n\n* Fix pagination\n\n* Update test\n\n* Add payment status filter\n\n* Capture server logs in e2e workflow\n\n* Implement server-side search with debounced pagination\n\n- Add patient name search parameter to usePaginatedBills hook\n- Remove client-side sorting (backend sorts by ID descending)\n- Add 300ms debounce to search input using useDebounce\n- Keep filter dropdown visible during loading and error states\n- Fix search UI alignment with proper flexbox layout\n- Move `mapLineItems` helper outside component scope\n- Update tests to verify backend API calls with search params\n\n* Increase debounce delay to 5ms\n\n* Improve pagination UX and search accessibility\n\n- Fix page size change to reset to page 1 for predictable navigation\n- Improve loading states: show skeleton only on initial load, spinner on subsequent loads\n- Optimize search input labels: use descriptive placeholder for visibility\n- Update tests to use Testing Library best practices (role-based queries)\n- Add test coverage for smart loading states and page size behavior\n\nUX improvements:\n- Search placeholder now shows \"Filter bills by patient name or identifier\"\n- Search label simplified to \"Search for a patient\" (screen reader only)\n- Users keep context during pagination/filtering with non-blocking spinner\n- Page size changes predictably return to first page\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>","authorName":"Nethmi Rodrigo","authorEmail":"nethmi@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"46488b5985565bb60a83ca787f83d6c84fde12b7","date":"2025-11-07T11:18:48+03:00","message":"(test) O3-5164: Add billing dashboard workflow test and refactor test structure (#508)","refs":"","body":"* (test) O3-5164: Add billing dashboard workflow test and refactor test structure\n\nAdds comprehensive E2E test suite for the billing dashboard workflow covering the following scenarios:\n\n- Navigation to billing dashboard\n- Display of pending bills\n- Payment processing\n- Status updates (bills transitioning from PENDING to PAID)\n- Bill movement between pending and paid filters in the Bill List table\n\nIt also refactors the test structure to be more modular and easier to maintain. Specifically, this involves:\n\n- Splitting billing tests into separate files by workflow:\n  * billing-patient-chart.spec.ts: Patient Chart workflow\n  * billing-dashboard.spec.ts: Billing Dashboard workflow\n- Replacing try-finally cleanup with canonical test.afterEach hooks\n- Adding error handling in cleanup to prevent failures from blocking other cleanup\n\nAlso adds a new BillingDashboardPage page object for handling the billing dashboard UI interactions.\n\n* Fixup","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"272d0cf00df3501843a41b5f4a1f8c5354e6a62b","date":"2025-10-24T20:16:54+03:00","message":"(feat) O3-5142: Prevent duplicate payment mode selection","refs":"","body":"* (feat) O3-5142: Prevent duplicate payment mode selection\n\n* Added helper function for filtering selected payment modes\n\n* Optimize payment mode filter and add tests\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>","authorName":"abertnamanya","authorEmail":"abertnamanya@gmail.com"},{"hash":"2d7d11b33cb14b70a62df5db1a6675bf29c5a134","date":"2025-10-16T12:02:15+03:00","message":"(feat) Standardize translation strings and improve consistency (#440)","refs":"","body":"- Convert all translation keys to sentence case\n- Replace \"e.g.\" with \"For example\" for better internationalization\n- Fix concatenation issues (filterBy, noResultsFor, paymentModeName)\n- Consolidate duplicate translation keys\n- Remove ellipses from loading states for consistency\n- Update test assertions to use case-insensitive regex patterns\n- Add missing translation keys for hardcoded strings\n- Fix grammatical errors and improve semantic clarity","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"9c12676f7dd257f47f5ff22f4055fd6e0fd05ee9","date":"2025-10-15T21:55:32+03:00","message":"(fix) Exclude voided items from bill calculations (#437)","refs":"","body":"* (fix) Exclude voided items from bill calculations\n\nVoided (soft-deleted) line items were being included in bill totals,\nstatus calculations, and item lists, causing incorrect amounts and\nmisleading bill statuses.\n\nChanges:\n- Filter voided items in mapBillProperties before all calculations\n- Use calculateTotalAmount helper in bill waiver (includes voided check)\n- Refactor promise chains to async/await with try/catch/finally\n- Improve URL building in useBills with server-side status filtering\n- Add currency formatting for all price displays\n- Translate hardcoded strings in billing checkin form\n- Add accessibility improvements (aria-live on dynamic totals)\n- Remove unused code and imports\n\nTests:\n- Fix edit-bill-item tests broken by currency formatting changes\n- Add form validation test coverage for quantity constraints\n- Verify validation errors appear/clear correctly\n- Ensure submission is blocked with invalid data\n\nImpact: Bills with voided items will now show correct totals and status.\nPreviously, a fully paid bill could incorrectly show as PENDING if it\ncontained voided items.\n\n* Additional fix: register edit bill line item modal using modal system","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"ec51b0fd94dcc01269815b85afd13e373bb1a3ba","date":"2024-09-18T09:50:44+03:00","message":"O3-3810(Enhancement) Filter on billing dashboard to correctly reflect the payment status (#53)","refs":"","body":"* O3-3810(Enhancement)Filter the billing dashboard to correctly reflect the payment status\r\n\r\n* test failure\r\n\r\n* Remove comments","authorName":"AJAL ODORA JONATHAN","authorEmail":"43242517+ODORA0@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"a0b769f0b2e4b1ccee39dd0bbcf4f9614ce54e0c","date":"2024-05-22T14:22:42+03:00","message":"(Enhancement) Filter by should default to Pending Bills (#47)","refs":"","body":"* (Enhancement) Filter by should default to Pending Bills\r\n\r\n* Fix Failing test","authorName":"AJAL ODORA JONATHAN","authorEmail":"43242517+ODORA0@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"473bc5d74f0d34ce6ce632bb17b3e40651c3fd89","date":"2024-04-02T12:43:04+03:00","message":"(refactor) Update filtering of patients bill to endpoint (#32)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"CynthiaKamau","authorEmail":"cynthiakamau54@gmail.com"}],"totalCount":13}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d7367715-0468-4212-b549-e8206d8177ba","uuid":"b390f851-d016-4cfd-b7ff-0fa7d22721f9","timestamp":"2026-10-24T04:19:10.415Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"hash":"6e4cdcd9db634a947b317df793d5b8170a9768e9","date":"2026-09-17T20:43:12+05:30","message":"(feat) Add date range filter to bills table (#831)","refs":"","body":"* (feat) Add date range filter to bills table\n\n* (feat) Guard inverted date range and show Clear dates only when a date is set\n\nSkip the bill fetch when the end date is before the start date and show\nthe picker's invalid text instead, since the backend rejects that range\nwith a 400. Render the Clear dates button only when a date is set. Raise\nthe billing backend floor to 2.5.0-0, which is the version that adds the\nstartDate and endDate search parameters.\n\n* (fix) Skip the bills request for an inverted date range and let the date controls wrap","authorName":"Nethmi Rodrigo","authorEmail":"nethmi@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"e8126b39dc10bcdc719250b004afe86f7782f36a","date":"2026-06-04T14:23:05+05:30","message":"(feat) O3-5413: Add bill refunds (#738)","refs":"","body":"* feat(refunds): add bill refunds feature\n\n- Cashiers can request refunds on PAID/PARTIALLY_REFUNDED bills; admins approve or reject; cashiers then process approved refunds to COMPLETED\n- Supports bill-level and line-item-scoped refunds with cumulative cap enforcement; at most one active refund per scope at a time\n- Adds admin Refund Requests page, cashier Request Refund modal, and admin Review Bill Refunds modal with receipt rail showing approved and completed refund totals\n- Fixes: REJECTED refunds were incorrectly reducing remainingRefundable; COMPLETED refunds were not deducted from line-item remaining (double-refund risk); bill.refunds?.filter().reduce() crashed when refunds was undefined\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(refunds): add pending refunds filter to bills table\n\nAdds REFUND_REQUESTED to BillStatus and a 'Pending refunds' filter option in the bills table to surface bills awaiting refund processing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(refunds): address SonarCloud issues in refunds feature\n\n- Extract deeply nested onRefundRequest/onClick callbacks into named functions\n- Replace chained ternaries with if/else block before JSX return\n- Add null guard in handleRequestRefund to remove non-null assertions\n- Use flatMap for type-safe lineItemUuid set construction\n- Remove unnecessary `as RefundStatus` cast (type already narrows correctly)\n- Replace role=\"progressbar\" on div with aria-busy=\"true\"\n- Mark component props interfaces as readonly\n- Replace window with globalThis in test files\n- Remove unused showSnackbar and useOpenmrsFetchAll imports\n- Replace parseFloat with Number.parseFloat\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(refunds): remove unnecessary non-null assertion in handleLineItemRefundRequest\n\nAdd early return guard for item.uuid so TypeScript narrows the type,\nmaking the ! assertion redundant and satisfying SonarCloud S4325.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(refunds): keep review modal open on action and fix multi-line refund eligibility\n\n- Review modal now refreshes bill data in place instead of closing after approve/reject\n- Bills in REFUND_REQUESTED status can now accept refund requests on unaffected line items\n- Add unit tests covering all refund eligibility scenarios (bill-level and line-level blocking)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(refunds): mock billing.resource in review-bill-refunds modal test\n\nuseBill was added to the modal but the test's esm-framework mock did not\nexpose openmrsFetch, causing the test suite to fail on push.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(refunds): resolve duplicate translation key and add voided discount test\n\n- Align refundAmount translation value to 'Refund amount' across all usages\n- Add test asserting voided discounts are not rendered in DiscountsTable\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(refunds): add void action to refund review card\n\nAdmins can now void any refund regardless of status. Follows the same\ninline-confirm pattern as the discount card's delete action.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(refunds): improve refund review modal and validation\n\n- Rename `busy` → `processingRefundId`/`disabled` in RefundCard and RefundReviewStack for clearer semantics\n- Add per-line-item refund cap validation before approving\n- Fix over-approval guard to exclude the refund being approved from committed total\n- Show progress bar alongside content instead of replacing it during loading\n- Add inline error state when bill data fails to load\n- Guard against null netAmount in invoice refund handler\n- Switch requestRefundModal and reviewBillRefundsModal to async lifecycle\n- Make MappedBill.netAmount non-optional\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(refunds): reconcile summary card figures when discount and prior refunds exist\n\nShow amountAfterDiscount as the bill-level scope total in the summary card, and\nadd an 'Already refunded' row (hidden when zero) so all three figures always\nadd up visually regardless of discounts or prior refunds on the same bill.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Cleanup props\n\n* feat(refunds): show tooltip on disabled Request refund button\n\nWraps the button in a Carbon Tooltip (only when disabled) to explain\nthat a line-item refund is already in progress, and adds unit tests\ncovering the disabled state and tooltip label.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(refunds): surface void as delete in UI and add coverage for line-item and void flows\n\nReplaces all user-facing \"void\" language with \"delete\" to match the\nconvention used for discounts, line items, and bills. Adds tests for\nline-item-scoped refund approval (including the exceeds-line-total\nguard) and the full delete confirmation flow.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(refunds): show already-refunded row for line items with prior completed refunds\n\nComputes alreadyRefunded symmetrically for line-item refunds using\nscopeTotal - remainingRefundable, matching the bill-level calculation.\nThe summary card now shows the \"Already refunded\" row whenever a line\nitem has prior completed refunds, making the figures add up correctly.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(refunds): close concurrent-action races and i18n gaps\n\n- Disable Approve/Confirm reject/Confirm delete across all cards while\n  any request is in flight (was only guarding the active card's UUID)\n- Add tests covering cross-card Approve and Confirm-reject lock-out\n- Remove dead useBillRefunds export and its test block\n- Add extraction hint block + en.json keys for all BillStatus values\n  so the receipt-rail status tag never falls back to raw enum strings\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(refunds): remove redundant non-null assertions flagged by SonarCloud\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(refunds): suppress false invalid state on empty NumberInput on open\n\nAdd allowEmpty to the NumberInput in the refund and discount modals so\nCarbon's internal emptiness check does not trigger the red invalid state\nbefore the user has typed anything. Submit gating is unaffected.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(refunds): keep confirmation footer contained at narrow modal widths\n\nSplit confirmation copy from its button group into a wrapping flex row so\nthe text and controls stack vertically rather than overflow at narrow widths.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","authorName":"Nethmi Rodrigo","authorEmail":"nethmi@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"276998ab31efde52652f58a4a22e099970ca615f","date":"2026-05-06T03:05:16+05:30","message":"(feat) Default bills table filter to \"Pending confirmation\" (#727)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Nethmi Rodrigo","authorEmail":"nethmi@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"6e3d447cbfade14f3ec4b73d1697daf8f203bf79","date":"2026-02-13T16:17:05+05:30","message":"(fix) Delete line items from a bill (#617)","refs":"","body":"The billing tables had several inconsistencies: the \"Visit time\" column\nwas misleadingly named (it's actually `dateCreated`), there was no\nreceipt/invoice number column for navigating to invoices, the patient\nname was a link to the invoice page (unintuitive), and the billed items\ndisplay had a trailing \"&\" when a line item lacked a name.\n\n- Rename \"Visit time\" to \"Bill date\" across all billing tables\n- Add \"Invoice number\" column linking to the invoice page in the bill\n  list, bill history, and patient bills tables\n- Remove clickable link from patient name in the bill list table\n- Rename \"Bill code\" to \"Invoice number\" in the invoice line items table\n- Fix trailing \"&\" in billed items by replacing reduce with\n  map/filter/join\n- Update unit tests and e2e tests to reflect the new column structure\n","authorName":"Nethmi Rodrigo","authorEmail":"nethmi@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"e734a4221aead9c6787cec024a58782c84452cb7","date":"2026-02-07T01:56:14+03:00","message":"(fix) Add invoice number column and fix billed items display","refs":"","body":"The billing tables had several inconsistencies: the \"Visit time\" column\nwas misleadingly named (it's actually `dateCreated`), there was no\nreceipt/invoice number column for navigating to invoices, the patient\nname was a link to the invoice page (unintuitive), and the billed items\ndisplay had a trailing \"&\" when a line item lacked a name.\n\n- Rename \"Visit time\" to \"Bill date\" across all billing tables\n- Add \"Invoice number\" column linking to the invoice page in the bill\n  list, bill history, and patient bills tables\n- Remove clickable link from patient name in the bill list table\n- Rename \"Bill code\" to \"Invoice number\" in the invoice line items table\n- Fix trailing \"&\" in billed items by replacing reduce with\n  map/filter/join\n- Update unit tests and e2e tests to reflect the new column structure\n","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"a71eed142190dcdab9199d02e27bc1ef49d71933","date":"2025-11-24T18:15:29+05:30","message":"(fix) Use server-side pagination when fetching bills (#504)","refs":"","body":"* (fix): Use pagination when fetching bills\n\n* Fix pagination\n\n* Update test\n\n* Add payment status filter\n\n* Capture server logs in e2e workflow\n\n* Implement server-side search with debounced pagination\n\n- Add patient name search parameter to usePaginatedBills hook\n- Remove client-side sorting (backend sorts by ID descending)\n- Add 300ms debounce to search input using useDebounce\n- Keep filter dropdown visible during loading and error states\n- Fix search UI alignment with proper flexbox layout\n- Move `mapLineItems` helper outside component scope\n- Update tests to verify backend API calls with search params\n\n* Increase debounce delay to 5ms\n\n* Improve pagination UX and search accessibility\n\n- Fix page size change to reset to page 1 for predictable navigation\n- Improve loading states: show skeleton only on initial load, spinner on subsequent loads\n- Optimize search input labels: use descriptive placeholder for visibility\n- Update tests to use Testing Library best practices (role-based queries)\n- Add test coverage for smart loading states and page size behavior\n\nUX improvements:\n- Search placeholder now shows \"Filter bills by patient name or identifier\"\n- Search label simplified to \"Search for a patient\" (screen reader only)\n- Users keep context during pagination/filtering with non-blocking spinner\n- Page size changes predictably return to first page\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>","authorName":"Nethmi Rodrigo","authorEmail":"nethmi@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"46488b5985565bb60a83ca787f83d6c84fde12b7","date":"2025-11-07T11:18:48+03:00","message":"(test) O3-5164: Add billing dashboard workflow test and refactor test structure (#508)","refs":"","body":"* (test) O3-5164: Add billing dashboard workflow test and refactor test structure\n\nAdds comprehensive E2E test suite for the billing dashboard workflow covering the following scenarios:\n\n- Navigation to billing dashboard\n- Display of pending bills\n- Payment processing\n- Status updates (bills transitioning from PENDING to PAID)\n- Bill movement between pending and paid filters in the Bill List table\n\nIt also refactors the test structure to be more modular and easier to maintain. Specifically, this involves:\n\n- Splitting billing tests into separate files by workflow:\n  * billing-patient-chart.spec.ts: Patient Chart workflow\n  * billing-dashboard.spec.ts: Billing Dashboard workflow\n- Replacing try-finally cleanup with canonical test.afterEach hooks\n- Adding error handling in cleanup to prevent failures from blocking other cleanup\n\nAlso adds a new BillingDashboardPage page object for handling the billing dashboard UI interactions.\n\n* Fixup","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"272d0cf00df3501843a41b5f4a1f8c5354e6a62b","date":"2025-10-24T20:16:54+03:00","message":"(feat) O3-5142: Prevent duplicate payment mode selection","refs":"","body":"* (feat) O3-5142: Prevent duplicate payment mode selection\n\n* Added helper function for filtering selected payment modes\n\n* Optimize payment mode filter and add tests\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>","authorName":"abertnamanya","authorEmail":"abertnamanya@gmail.com"},{"hash":"2d7d11b33cb14b70a62df5db1a6675bf29c5a134","date":"2025-10-16T12:02:15+03:00","message":"(feat) Standardize translation strings and improve consistency (#440)","refs":"","body":"- Convert all translation keys to sentence case\n- Replace \"e.g.\" with \"For example\" for better internationalization\n- Fix concatenation issues (filterBy, noResultsFor, paymentModeName)\n- Consolidate duplicate translation keys\n- Remove ellipses from loading states for consistency\n- Update test assertions to use case-insensitive regex patterns\n- Add missing translation keys for hardcoded strings\n- Fix grammatical errors and improve semantic clarity","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"9c12676f7dd257f47f5ff22f4055fd6e0fd05ee9","date":"2025-10-15T21:55:32+03:00","message":"(fix) Exclude voided items from bill calculations (#437)","refs":"","body":"* (fix) Exclude voided items from bill calculations\n\nVoided (soft-deleted) line items were being included in bill totals,\nstatus calculations, and item lists, causing incorrect amounts and\nmisleading bill statuses.\n\nChanges:\n- Filter voided items in mapBillProperties before all calculations\n- Use calculateTotalAmount helper in bill waiver (includes voided check)\n- Refactor promise chains to async/await with try/catch/finally\n- Improve URL building in useBills with server-side status filtering\n- Add currency formatting for all price displays\n- Translate hardcoded strings in billing checkin form\n- Add accessibility improvements (aria-live on dynamic totals)\n- Remove unused code and imports\n\nTests:\n- Fix edit-bill-item tests broken by currency formatting changes\n- Add form validation test coverage for quantity constraints\n- Verify validation errors appear/clear correctly\n- Ensure submission is blocked with invalid data\n\nImpact: Bills with voided items will now show correct totals and status.\nPreviously, a fully paid bill could incorrectly show as PENDING if it\ncontained voided items.\n\n* Additional fix: register edit bill line item modal using modal system","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"ec51b0fd94dcc01269815b85afd13e373bb1a3ba","date":"2024-09-18T09:50:44+03:00","message":"O3-3810(Enhancement) Filter on billing dashboard to correctly reflect the payment status (#53)","refs":"","body":"* O3-3810(Enhancement)Filter the billing dashboard to correctly reflect the payment status\r\n\r\n* test failure\r\n\r\n* Remove comments","authorName":"AJAL ODORA JONATHAN","authorEmail":"43242517+ODORA0@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"a0b769f0b2e4b1ccee39dd0bbcf4f9614ce54e0c","date":"2024-05-22T14:22:42+03:00","message":"(Enhancement) Filter by should default to Pending Bills (#47)","refs":"","body":"* (Enhancement) Filter by should default to Pending Bills\r\n\r\n* Fix Failing test","authorName":"AJAL ODORA JONATHAN","authorEmail":"43242517+ODORA0@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"473bc5d74f0d34ce6ce632bb17b3e40651c3fd89","date":"2024-04-02T12:43:04+03:00","message":"(refactor) Update filtering of patients bill to endpoint (#32)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"CynthiaKamau","authorEmail":"cynthiakamau54@gmail.com"}],"totalCount":13}"}],"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_018ATuw59FhBG1oCSNQRRwfS","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
