e dates are sent as the `startDate` and `endDate` search parameters on `GET /billing/bill`, which the billing backend added in openmrs/openmrs-module-billing#193.\n\n- `usePaginatedBills` appends `startDate` (start of day) and `endDate` (end of day) to the URL when set.\n- The From picker is capped by the To date and the To picker floored by the From date. When a typed range is inverted, `usePaginatedBills` passes a `null` URL so no request is made (the backend would return a 400); the To picker shows an invalid message and the table shows the \"No matching bills\" state.\n- A Clear dates button appears once a date is set and resets both dates.\n- The `billing` backend dependency floor in `routes.json` is raised to `>=2.5.0-0`, the first version with the new search parameters.\n\n## Screenshots\n<!-- Required if you are making UI changes. -->\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6822335b-af02-4bcb-a0f8-03dde54c33cb\n\n\n\n## Related Issue\n<!-- Paste the link to the Jira ticket here if one exists. -->\n<!-- https://issues.openmrs.org/browse/O3- -->\n\n## Other\n<!-- Anything not covered above -->\n\nTwo standalone `OpenmrsDatePicker`s are used rather than `OpenmrsDateRangePicker` because the filter needs to support open-ended ranges (only a From date, or only a To date). The range picker only emits a value once both ends are set.\n\n","comments":[{"kind":"issue_comment","author":"greptile-apps","createdAt":"2026-09-10T12:31:10.000Z","state":null,"path":null,"line":null,"body":"<!-- greptile_summary -->\n\n<h2><a href=\"https://app.greptile.com/api/retrigger?id=62572270\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/RetriggerDark.svg?v=1\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/Retrigger.svg?v=1\"><img alt=\"Retrigger\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/Retrigger.svg?v=1\" align=\"right