his code passes `null` for both filters. That removes both query constraints and displays unrelated bills as though they matched the visible range. Suppress the request, retain the last valid results, or reconcile the displayed selections before fetching.\n\n<details><summary><strong>Artifacts</strong></summary><br />\n\n**[Evidence from the check](https://app.greptile.com/trex/artifacts/8d6839ea-0197-479a-8b45-b51c824b189a)**\n\n- The exact authored Vitest harness changes From and To to an inverted range, records fetch arguments, and asserts the rendered picker and bill-result state; it deterministically demonstrates the state/request mismatch.\n\n**[Evidence from the check](https://app.greptile.com/trex/artifacts/463031a2-c1e5-43b2-a4b8-cf4e85d30110)**\n\n- The exact authored shell command runs the focused harness and records its command, working directory, exit code, and Vitest output; it provides repeatable execution.\n\n**[Command output from the check](https://app.greptile.com/trex/artifacts/054cad5e-0a96-4f74-b218-7cbb1d656131)**\n\n- The focused harness executed against the parent revision and passed while asserting the inverted selected dates were forwarded to the fetch hook; it establishes the before behavior.\n\n**[Command output from the check](https://app.greptile.com/trex/artifacts/0dc73cdd-69a9-4ffa-a8ee-d121056506d3)**\n\n- The focused harness executed against PR #831 and passed while asserting null request dates, populated pickers, and the unrelated unfiltered fixture result; it confirms the finding.\n\n<a href=\"https://app.greptile.com/trex/runs/23570321/artifacts?artifact=8d6839ea-0197-479a-8b45-b51c824b189a\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.co"},{"kind":"review_comment","author":"greptile-apps","createdAt":"2026-09-10T12:31:13.000Z","state":null,"path":"src/bills-table/bills-table.scss","line":55,"body":"<a href=\"#\"><img alt=\"P2\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p2.svg?v=9\" align=\"top\"></a> **Date controls overflow mobile**\n\nOn a 320px viewport, selecting a date reveals the clear action but leaves the non-wrapping controls 433px wide, placing the Clear dates button outside the viewport. This is a non-blocking usability concern: mobile users may be unable to clear their selected dates. Allow the controls to wrap or stack at narrow widths.\n\nNote: If this suggestion doesn't match your team's coding style, reply to this and let me know. I'll remember it for next time!\n\n<details><summary><strong>Artifacts</strong></summary><br />\n\n**[Evidence from the check](https://app.greptile.com/trex/artifacts/285b96af-aeaf-4347-a7f3-6047182752cb)**\n\n- The exact authored Playwright harness.\n\n**[Command output from the check](https://app.greptile.com/trex/artifacts/3896d22c-8c1b-4da1-aa0f-167e36319af4)**\n\n- The command, working directory, exit code 0, and before/after measurements.\n\n**[Command output from the check](https://app.greptile.com/trex/artifacts/8b83277b-a484-47b1-bdda-224e5a207e10)**\n\n- The parent-state measurement.\n\n**[Command output from the check](https://app.greptile.com/trex/artifacts/47a16f80-24b0-4248-b936-2953228e47a2)**\n\n- The selected-date PR-state measurement.\n\n**[▶ Date controls before selection](https://app.greptile.com/trex/artifacts/509c6448-2ba2-4766-a4d0-055326af3e55)**\n\n- The narrow viewport recording shows the initial date-control layout before a date is selected.\n\n**[Date controls before selection](https://app.greptile.com/trex/artifacts/91ba6072-1589-4cd9-9ad3-6abdfa5728b9)**\n\n- The poster frame shows the initial narrow viewport layout.\n\n**[▶ Clear action outside viewport](https://app.greptile.com/trex/artifacts/fe8cba22-da35-42ca-8106-e9dac6d12e3f)**\n\n- The narrow viewport recording shows that selecting a date reveals a Clear dates action outside the visible area.\n\n**[Clear action outside viewport](https://app.greptile.com/tr"},{"kind":"review","a